 "verdict": "CONTROL (the rung, read first): shape separates ORDERED from the rest on 3 of 4 scalars (['area', 'fill', 'curvature']), against F36's ignition probability at p = 0.0000, d = 3.03. Shape reproduces a separation that is known to exist, so it is measuring dynamics. PRIMARY: edge vs chaotic separates on 0 of 4 shape scalars (none), where ignition probability gives p = 0.47. No shape scalar separates them either. The 3-class ordering fails a fourth time, and shape inherits ignition's ceiling -- it is not a finer discriminator of dynamical class, which bounds what it can be used for on a language model. BOUNDARY: ECA is deterministic and binary; a language-model lattice is stochastic over a large vocabulary. A shape statistic validated here is licensed as a DYNAMICAL discriminator, not automatically as a model-facing one.",
